  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4520",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\n\"We found that not only was it a civil war, an effort by a people who had for years been seeking their liberation from any colonial influence whatsoever, but also we found that the Vietnamese whom we had enthusiastically molded after our own image were hard put to take up the fight against the threat we were supposedly saving them from.\n\"We found most people didn't even know the difference between communism and democracy. They only wanted to work in rice paddies without helicopters strafing them and bombs with napalm burning their villages and tearing their country apart. They wanted everything to do with the war, particularly with this foreign presence of the United States of America, to leave them alone in peace, and they practiced the art of survival by siding with whichever military force was present at a particular time, be it Viet Cong, North Vietnamese or American.\"\nJohn Kerry, 1971\nThe conflict described above is most likely a result of which of the following doctrines?\n\nOptions: \nA. Wilsonianism\nB. Containment\nC. Big-stick diplomacy\nD. Monroe Doctrine\nE. Isolationism\nF. Domino Theory\nG. Marshall Plan\nH. Truman Doctrine\nI. Manifest Destiny\nJ. Imperialism\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "agnes-2.0-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The quote describes the Vietnam War, where the United States intervened to prevent the spread of communism in Southeast Asia. This intervention was driven by the Cold War policy of **Containment**, which aimed to stop communist expansion globally. While the Domino Theory (Option F) provided the specific rationale for Vietnam, Containment (Option B) is the broader overarching doctrine that justified US involvement in such conflicts during the Cold War.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
      "success": true,
