      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is B. Genetic evidence indicates that japonica and indica rice are more closely related to their respective local wild ancestors (Oryza rufipogon) in East/Southeast Asia and South Asia, respectively, rather than to each other. This supports the hypothesis of independent, separate domestication events for these two primary varieties.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
