      "generated_answer": "The Sumerian text from the Epic of Gilgamesh presents a dark, gloomy afterlife where the dead dwell in darkness, eat dirt, and have no light. The Egyptian text from the Maxims of Ptahhotep presents a more positive view, suggesting that truth and righteousness lead to divine guidance and successful passage through life. \n\nThe question asks which conclusion is best supported, and the most direct comparison is the view of the afterlife shown in both texts.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
