      "generated_answer": "The markings found on the mud-bricks of Huaca del Sol are widely interpreted by archaeologists as stamps or signs used to identify the specific local communities or labor groups responsible for producing them. This practice helped organize the massive construction effort by attributing work to specific units. Therefore, the markings were not random or instructional notes, but rather identifiers of origin.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
