      "generated_answer": "The passage highlights a \"long\" wait and the merchant's uncertainty about when he can return home, indicating that the primary source of strain is the physical distance and extended separation inherent in medieval trade networks. While financial status is mentioned as a factor for his return, the overarching context describes the difficulties faced by families due to long-distance commerce. Therefore, the most probable cause is the strain placed on merchant families by long periods of separation.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
      "success": true,
