    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4644",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\n\"I observe the great and wonderful mistake, both our own and our fathers, as to the civil powers of this world, acting in spiritual matters. I have read…the last will and testament of the Lord Jesus over many times, and yet I cannot find by one tittle of that testament that if He had been pleased to have accepted of a temporal crown and government that ever He would have put forth the least finger of temporal or civil power in the matters of His spiritual affairs and Kingdom. Hence must it lamentably be against the testimony of Christ Jesus for the civil state to impose upon the souls of the people a religion, a worship, a ministry, oaths (in religious and civil affairs), tithes, times, days, marryings, and buryings in holy ground…\"\nRoger Williams, The Hireling Ministry None of Christ's, 1652\nPuritan emigration from England came to a near halt between the years 1649 and 1660 because, during that period,\n\nOptions: \nA. most Puritans converted to Catholicism\nB. the New England settlement had become too overcrowded, and colonial legislatures strongly discouraged immigration\nC. the Puritans controlled the English government\nD. there was a severe outbreak of disease in New England, discouraging immigration\nE. most English Puritans were imprisoned for heresy\nF. the Puritans were persecuted and fled to other parts of Europe\nG. the English government banned all emigration\nH. the Puritans were engaged in a civil war in England\nI. the New England settlements were destroyed by Native American tribes\nJ. the English government offered incentives for Puritans to stay in England\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "agnes-2.0-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The period between 1649 and 1660 corresponds to the English Civil War and the subsequent Interregnum under Oliver Cromwell, during which the Puritans held significant political power in England. Because they controlled the government, there was no longer a pressing need to flee religious persecution in England, leading to a halt in emigration to New England. Therefore, the correct answer is that the Puritans controlled the English government.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 671,
        "output_tokens": 98,
        "total_tokens": 769
      },
      "provider": "agnes",
      "error": null
