      "generated_answer": "The First Great Awakening was a religious revival movement in the American colonies that emerged in reaction against the growing influence of rationalism and secularism associated with the Enlightenment. Therefore, it is best understood as a response to the intellectual trends of that era.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
