      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}\n\nThe expectation in Source 1 was that uniting Venezuela and New Granada would lead to greater power and prosperity, but this relied on overcoming local divisions. Sectionalism among regional elites often prioritized local interests over national unity, leading to the eventual dissolution of Gran Colombia and undermining the goal of a strong, unified republic.",
