      "generated_answer": "The most historically significant factor was that the Inca Empire was fractured by a recent civil war between brothers Atahualpa and Huáscar, which severely weakened their ability to resist the Spanish conquest. While other factors like disease and alliances with indigenous groups played a role, the immediate political instability caused by the civil war was the primary reason Pizarro succeeded.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
