      "generated_answer": "The first verse from the Qur'an prohibits alcohol and gambling, labeling them as \"infamy\" and instructing believers to abstain to achieve success, which aligns with a strict moral code. This prohibitionist stance is best described as a puritanical injunction against behaviors deemed sinful or distracting from spiritual goals. Therefore, the tone reflects a demand for adherence to specific behavioral restrictions rather than celebration, mysticism, or political commentary.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
