      "generated_answer": "Based on archaeological consensus, the concentration of wealth (social stratification) is considered a defining and common characteristic of civilizations, whereas warfare varies significantly in frequency and intensity across different societies. While warfare often accompanies wealth concentration, it is not universally present or strictly proportional in all cases, making option E the most accurate general statement.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
