      "generated_answer": "The excerpt highlights Queen Victoria's concern about her health due to social obligations and mentions the conclusion of political negotiations with the Tories, implying that her role was largely ceremonial while real political power resided with ministers like Lord Melbourne. This suggests that despite the busy social calendar, the monarchy itself did not wield direct political authority.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
