      "generated_answer": "The discrepancy between early migrant skulls and modern Native American skulls suggests that physical characteristics like skull shape can undergo significant changes over time due to factors such as genetic drift, environmental adaptation, or population mixing, rather than indicating a lack of ancestry. This implies that the early migrants likely did contribute to the genetic pool, but their cranial morphology evolved or changed drastically over subsequent generations. Therefore, the most reasonable conclusion among the choices is that skull shapes are not static and can change dramatically.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
