      "generated_answer": "The Holocene epoch is characterized by significant cultural developments worldwide, including the rise of agriculture and complex societies, but it did not result in a single global civilization or a new ice age. While megafauna extinctions occurred in many regions, they were not complete globally, and farming was not introduced to Australia from neighbors but developed independently or arrived much later. Therefore, the most accurate shared feature among the options is the general trend of increasing cultural diversity and social complexity.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
