      "generated_answer": "\nHere is a Python function that performs the task described in the prompt. The function reads from standard input and outputs the result. It uses Kruskal's algorithm to find the minimum spanning tree (MST) of the graph if it is connected.\n\n```python\nfrom sys import stdin\nfrom heapq import heappop, heappush\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\ndef find(parent, x):\n    if parent[x] != x:\n        parent[x] = find(parent, parent[x])\n    return parent[x]\n\ndef union(parent, rank, x, y):\n    rootX = find(parent, x)\n    rootY = find(parent, y)\n    if rootX != rootY:\n        if rank[rootX] > rank[rootY]:\n            parent[rootY] = rootX\n        elif rank[rootX] < rank[rootY]:\n            parent[rootX] = rootY\n        else:\n            parent[rootY] = rootX\n            rank[rootX] += 1\n\ndef main():\n    input = stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    idx = 0\n    N = int(data[idx])\n    idx += 1\n    M = int(data[idx])\n    idx += 1\n    \n    parent = list(range(N + 1))\n    rank = [0] * (N + 1)\n    \n    edges = []\n    for _ in range(M):\n        K = int(data[idx])\n        idx += 1\n        C = int(data[idx])\n        idx += 1\n        for j in range(K - 1):\n            u = int(data[idx])\n            idx += 1\n            v = int(data[idx])\n            idx += 1\n            heappush(edges, (C, u, v))\n    \n    mst_weight = 0\n    num_edges = 0\n    \n    while edges and num_edges < N - 1:\n        C, u, v = heappop(edges)\n        if find(parent, u) != find(parent, v):\n            union(parent, rank, u, v)\n            mst_weight += C\n            num_edges += 1\n    \n    if num_edges == N - 1:\n        print(mst_weight)\n    else:\n        print(-1)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\nTo run this function, you can provide the input through standard input. For example, you can save the input in a file and use it as follows:\n\n```sh\npython script.py < input.txt\n```\n\nThis will read the input from `input.txt` and print the output to standard output.",
