    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\n```python\ndef sum_of_power(nums):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    nums.sort()\n    n = len(nums)\n    prefix_sum = [0] * (n + 1)\n    for i in range(n):\n        prefix_sum[i + 1] = prefix_sum[i] + nums[i]\n\n    total_power = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        # Count how many times nums[i] is the maximum in a group\n        count_max = n - i\n        # Count how many times nums[i] is the minimum in a group\n        count_min = i + 1\n        # Calculate how many groups have nums[i] as the maximum and minimum\n        # which is equivalent to the number of ways to choose nums[i] as the maximum\n        # and the number of elements to the right of nums[i] as part of the group\n        num_groups = count_max * count_min\n        # Calculate the power of all these groups\n        group_power = pow(nums[i], 2, MOD) * nums[i] % MOD\n        # Add the contribution of these groups to the total power\n        total_power = (total_power + group_power * num_groups % MOD) % MOD\n\n    return total_power\n```",
