      "generated_answer": "\nHere's the Python function that fulfills the prompt's requirements:\n\n```python\ndef max_difference_trucks(n, weights):\n    weights.sort()\n    prefix_sum = [0] * (n + 1)\n    for i in range(n):\n        prefix_sum[i + 1] = prefix_sum[i] + weights[i]\n\n    max_diff = 0\n    for k in range(1, n + 1):\n        if n % k == 0:\n            num_trucks = n // k\n            min_load = prefix_sum[k] - prefix_sum[0]\n            max_load = prefix_sum[2*k] - prefix_sum[k]\n            diff = max_load - min_load\n            max_diff = max(max_diff, diff)\n\n    return max_diff\n\n# Read input from stdin\nimport sys\ninput = sys.stdin.read\ndata = input().split()\n\nindex = 0\nt = int(data[index])\nindex += 1\nresults = []\n\nfor _ in range(t):\n    n = int(data[index])\n    index += 1\n    weights = list(map(int, data[index:index + n]))\n    index += n\n\n    # Calculate the maximum absolute difference for this test case\n    max_diff = max_difference_trucks(n, weights)\n    results.append(max_diff)\n\n# Print results for all test cases\nfor result in results:\n    print(result)\n\n# Example of direct function call with sample input\n# To use this call, remove the input reading and results printing section above.\n# max_difference_trucks(2, [1, 2])\n```\n\nThis function reads the entire input at once, processes each test case by calling the `max_difference_trucks` function, and prints the results. The `max_difference_trucks` function sorts the weights array, computes prefix sums for quick range sum calculations, and iterates through all possible values of `k` to determine the maximum absolute difference. Note that this function assumes that the input is provided via standard input (stdin) as described in the prompt.",
