      "generated_answer": "\n```python\ndef min_coins_to_acquire_all_fruits(prices):\n    n = len(prices)\n    dp = [0] * n\n    dp[0] = prices[0]\n    \n    for i in range(1, n):\n        # Initialize with the cost of buying the current fruit\n        dp[i] = prices[i]\n        # Look back to find the minimum cost for the previous fruits\n        j = i - 1\n        while j >= 0:\n            # Check if the length of the free fruits from buying j is enough to include i\n            if j + i + 1 <= n:\n                dp[i] = min(dp[i], dp[j])\n            else:\n                break\n            j -= 1\n            \n    # The last fruit needs to be included in the total cost regardless of whether it's free or not\n    return sum(dp)\n```",
