      "generated_answer": "\n```python\nmod = 10**9+7\n\ndef count_sub_multisets(nums, l, r):\n    zeros_count = 0\n    non_zero_nums = []\n    for x in nums:\n        if x == 0:\n            zeros_count += 1\n        else:\n            non_zero_nums.append(x)\n    \n    if not non_zero_nums and zeros_count == 0:\n        # Only zeros, then the answer is zeros_count+1 if l==0, but need to check the range\n        if l <= 0 <= r:\n            return (zeros_count + 1) % mod\n        else:\n            return 0\n    \n    total_sum = sum(non_zero_nums)\n    from collections import defaultdict\n    freq = defaultdict(int)\n    for x in non_zero_nums:\n        freq[x] += 1\n\n    dp = [0] * (total_sum + 1)\n    dp[0] = 1\n\n    for x, f in freq.items():\n        new_dp = dp.copy()\n        for s in range(total_sum, -1, -1):\n            if s < x:\n                continue\n            temp_sum = 0\n            k = 1\n            while k <= f and s >= k * x:\n                temp_sum = (temp_sum + dp[s - k * x]) % mod\n                k += 1\n            new_dp[s] = (new_dp[s] + temp_sum) % mod\n        dp = new_dp\n\n    factor = zeros_count + 1\n    for i in range(total_sum + 1):\n        dp[i] = (dp[i] * factor) % mod\n\n    ans = 0\n    for s in range(l, r + 1):\n        if s <= total_sum:\n            ans = (ans + dp[s]) % mod\n\n    return ans\n```",
