    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. Return the function body without invoking it at the final solution. Question:\nYou are given an integer array prices representing the prices of various chocolates in a store. You are also given a single integer money, which represents your initial amount of money.\nYou must buy exactly two chocolates in such a way that you still have some non-negative leftover money. You would like to minimize the sum of the prices of the two chocolates you buy.\nReturn the amount of money you will have leftover after buying the two chocolates. If there is no way for you to buy two chocolates without ending up in debt, return money. Note that the leftover must be non-negative.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: prices = [1,2,2], money = 3\nOutput: 0\nExplanation: Purchase the chocolates priced at 1 and 2 units respectively. You will have 3 - 3 = 0 units of money afterwards. Thus, we return 0.\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: prices = [3,2,3], money = 3\nOutput: 3\nExplanation: You cannot buy 2 chocolates without going in debt, so we return 3.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n2 <= prices.length <= 50\n1 <= prices[i] <= 100\n1 <= money <= 100",
    "prediction": "MiniMax-M3",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Here is an efficient Python function that solves the problem:\n\n```python\ndef buyChoco(prices, money):\n    prices.sort()\n    n = len(prices)\n    min_sum = float('inf')\n    \n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        current_sum = prices[i] + prices[i + 1]\n        if current_sum <= money:\n            if current_sum < min_sum:\n                min_sum = current_sum\n    \n    if min_sum == float('inf'):\n        return money\n    return money - min_sum\n```\n\nThis solution:\n1. Sorts the prices array to allow efficient pair checking\n2. Iterates through adjacent pairs (the only candidates for minimum sum)\n3. Tracks the minimum valid sum that doesn't exceed money\n4. Returns the leftover money, or original money if no valid pair exists\n\n**Complexity Analysis:**\n- Time: O(n log n) due to sorting\n- Space: O(1) auxiliary space\n\nYou can also use a hash set approach for O(n) time complexity:\n\n```python\ndef buyChoco(prices, money):\n    seen = set()\n    min_sum = float('inf')\n    \n    for price in prices:\n        complement = money - price\n        # Try to find the smallest valid complement\n        for s in seen:\n            if s <= complement and s + price < min_sum:\n                min_sum = s + price\n        seen.add(price)\n    \n    return money - min_sum if min_sum != float('inf') else money\n```",
