      "generated_answer": "\n```python\ndef sum_of_powers(nums, k):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    n = len(nums)\n    nums.sort()\n    # Precompute the number of ways to choose (k-1) elements from (i-1) elements\n    # Using dynamic programming\n    combinations = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        combinations[0][i] = 1\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(i + 1):\n            combinations[i][j] = (combinations[i - 1][j] + combinations[i - 1][j - 1]) % MOD\n    # Compute prefix sums of nums to calculate the sum of elements in the subsequence\n    prefix_sum = [0] * (n + 1)\n    for i in range(n):\n        prefix_sum[i + 1] = prefix_sum[i] + nums[i]\n    total_power = 0\n    # For each element, compute the contribution to the total power\n    for i in range(n):\n        # Find the number of elements in the subsequence less than nums[i]\n        left = i\n        right = n\n        while left < right:\n            mid = (left + right + 1) // 2\n            if nums[mid] < nums[i]:\n                left = mid\n            else:\n                right = mid - 1\n        # Number of elements less than nums[i] is left\n        # Number of subsequences with k elements less than nums[i] is combinations[left][k - 1]\n        c_left = combinations[left][k - 1]\n        # Find the number of elements in the subsequence greater than nums[i]\n        left = i\n        right = n\n        while left < right:\n            mid = (left + right + 1) // 2\n            if nums[mid] > nums[i]:\n                right = mid - 1\n            else:\n                left = mid\n        # Number of elements greater than nums[i] is (n - right - 1)\n        # Number of subsequences with k elements greater than nums[i] is combinations[n - right - 1][k - 1]\n        c_right = combinations[n - right - 1][k - 1]\n        # Each subsequence with k elements contributes (nums[i] - nums[left]) * c_left * c_right\n        # and (nums[right] - nums[i]) * c_left * c_right to the total power\n        total_power = (total_power + (nums[i] - nums[left]) * c_left % MOD * c_right % MOD +\n                       (nums[right] - nums[i]) * c_left % MOD * c_right % MOD) % MOD\n    return total_power\n```",
