      "generated_answer": "In a conditional proposition \"if P, then Q,\" P is the antecedent. The statement is: \"The university raises tuition if, and only if, both the governor approves of it and the board of trustees recommends it.\" Rewritten in standard form: \"If (and only if both the governor approves and the board recommends), then the university raises tuition.\" Thus, the antecedent is the conjunction: \"the governor approves of it and the board of trustees recommends it.\"\n\nSince none of the options individually represent this conjunction, the antecedent is not listed.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
