    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\nThe correct dimensions that minimize the total cost for a cylindrical container with a volume of 10 cubic feet are r = 1.061 feet and h = 2.828 feet, which corresponds to option A. This is determined by minimizing the cost function C = 4πr² + 3πrh, subject to the volume constraint πr²h = 10. The derivative dC/dr = 8πr - 30/r² is set to zero, yielding r³ = 15/(4π) ≈ 1.1936, so r ≈ 1.061 feet, and h = 10/(πr²) ≈ 2.828 feet. Only option A satisfies the volume constraint and minimizes the cost.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
