    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_784",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Assuming that each lived for the term of the policy, compare the cost of a $5,000 20-payment life insurance policy for a young man 25 years of age with a man 45 years of age.\n\nOptions: \nA. $3649 and $2207\nB. $2207 and $5000\nC. $110.35 and $182.45\nD. $5000 and $5000\nE. $1500 and $2500\nF. $182.45 and $110.35\nG. $4250 and $6250\nH. $2207 and $3649\nI. $3649 and $3649\nJ. $2500 and $4500\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "MiniMax-M3",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to compare the total cost of a $5,000 20-payment life insurance policy for a 25-year-old versus a 45-year-old, assuming each lived for the term.\n\nThe cost of a 20-payment life policy equals the annual premium × 20 years. Since insurance premiums are significantly higher for older individuals due to greater mortality risk, the 25-year-old will pay less than the 45-year-old over the 20-year term.\n\nCalculating total costs (annual premium × 20):\n- Younger man (25): pays less over 20 years ≈ $110.35 × 20 = $2,207\n- Older man (45): pays more over 20 years ≈ $182.45 × 20 = $3,649\n\nThe 20-year cost for the 25-year-old is approximately $2,207, and for the 45-year-old is approximately $3,649.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
