    "prediction": "MiniMax-M3",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The **Competing Values Framework** (Cameron & Quinn) identifies four main culture types, and among them, **Role culture** is characterized by formal structures, clear hierarchies, standardized procedures, and a strong emphasis on efficiency, consistency, and stability.\n\n- Power culture (A) focuses on control and quick decisions.\n- Clan culture (B) emphasizes collaboration and family-like environments.\n- Network culture (C) is fluid and adaptive, prioritizing external connections.\n- Task culture (E) focuses on project-based, flexible problem-solving.\n- People culture (F) prioritizes individual needs over organizational goals.\n\nRole culture's bureaucratic and structured nature makes it the best fit for delivering **stability and efficiency**.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
