      "generated_answer": "Looking at this question about Vector Autoregression (VAR) models:\n\n- A is false: VAR coefficients are not always positive\n- B is false: VARs don't require same-sign variables\n- C and F are false: VAR coefficients typically lack clear theoretical interpretations\n- E and H are false: VARs can be used with stationary, non-stationary (cointegrated), or mixed variables\n- G is false: VARs are commonly used for forecasting\n- I is false: VARs often outperform univariate models by capturing interdependencies\n\n**D** is true: VARs often produce better forecasts than simultaneous equation structural models because they avoid the need to specify structural restrictions that may be misspecified, and they effectively capture dynamic relationships between variables.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
