      "generated_answer": "# Durbin-Watson Test Analysis\n\nFor a regression with 2 explanatory variables plus a constant and n=50, we need the critical values d_L and d_U at the 5% significance level. Approximately: d_L ≈ 1.46 and d_U ≈ 1.63.\n\nSince the test statistic DW = 1.53 falls in the range d_L < DW < d_U (1.46 < 1.53 < 1.63), the test is **inconclusive** — we cannot definitively reject or fail to reject the null hypothesis of no autocorrelation.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
