    "prediction": "MiniMax-M3",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The \"boomerang effect\" is a concept from **psychological reactance theory** (developed by Jack Brehm), where attempts to restrict a person's freedom actually cause them to want or do the restricted thing more.\n\nAn injunctive message (a normative statement about what *should* be done) can, paradoxically, trigger reactance and lead to the opposite of the intended outcome—such as increased likelihood of engaging in the discouraged behavior.\n\n\\boxed{Psychological reactance}",
