      "generated_answer": "The goal of blocking is to group similar experimental units together based on a variable that is associated with the response variable, to reduce variability and isolate the effect of the treatments being studied.\n\nSince daily exercise intensity (low, moderate, high) is associated with cholesterol level, and we want to determine the effect of fish oil vs. garlic capsules on cholesterol, blocking on exercise intensity would control for this known source of variation. Sleep length is not associated with cholesterol, so blocking on it would not be beneficial. The other variables (gender, diet, etc.) aren't mentioned as being associated with cholesterol in this context.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
