    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine if we can construct a cube with volume X times a given cube using compass and straightedge, we need X to be a perfect cube of a rational number (or a number expressible via field operations). Specifically, the new edge length would be ∛X times the original, which is constructible if and only if X is the cube of a constructible number (rational, since we start with one edge).\n\nChecking each value:\n- X=3: ∛3 is irrational, not constructible → 0\n- X=17: ∛17 is not rational → 0\n- X=8: ∛8 = 2, constructible → 1\n- X=27: ∛27 = 3, constructible → 1\n- X=343: ∛343 = 7, constructible → 1\n- X=1331: ∛1331 = 11, constructible → 1\n\nResult: [0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1]\n\n\\boxed{C}",
