      "generated_answer": "The 1:2:4 orbital resonance among the Galilean moons Io, Europa, and Ganymede means that for every orbit of Ganymede, Europa completes two orbits and Io completes four. This resonance causes tidal heating in Io, and importantly, it influences Io's orbit by making it slightly eccentric (elliptical), which drives the tidal bulging and volcanic activity.\n\nThe correct answer is **I. It makes the orbit of Io slightly elliptical.**\n\n\\boxed{I}",
