    "prediction": "MiniMax-M3",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We need to find $\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\{\\log\\frac{s+1}{s-1}\\}$ for $s > 1$.\n\nWrite $\\log\\frac{s+1}{s-1} = \\log(s+1) - \\log(s-1)$.\n\nUsing the property $\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\{F'(s)\\} = -t f(t)$, we differentiate:\n$$\\frac{d}{ds}\\log\\frac{s+1}{s-1} = \\frac{1}{s+1} - \\frac{1}{s-1} = \\frac{-2}{s^2-1}$$\n\nSo $\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{\\frac{-2}{s^2-1}\\right\\} = -2\\sinh t$, which means $\\frac{d}{ds}\\log\\frac{s+1}{s-1}$ inverts to $-2\\sinh t$.\n\nTherefore:\n$$\\log\\frac{s+1}{s-1} = -\\int_s^\\infty \\frac{-2}{p^2-1}\\,dp = 2\\int_s^\\infty \\frac{dp}{p^2-1}$$\n\nUsing $\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\{F(s)\\} = \\int_0^\\infty f(t)e^{-st}\\,dt$ with $F(s) = \\int_s^\\infty G(p)\\,dp$ where $\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\{G\\} = g(t)$:\n$$f(t) = \\frac{1}{t}g(t) = \\frac{-2\\sinh t}{t}$$\n\nWait, let me reconsider. Since $\\frac{d}{ds}\\log\\frac{s+1}{s-1}$ has inverse $-2\\sinh t$, and $\\log\\frac{s+1}{s-1} = -\\int_s^\\infty \\left(\\frac{1}{p+1}-\\frac{1}{p-1}\\right)dp$... \n\nActually, the inversion of $-\\frac{2}{s^2-1}$ is $-2\\sinh t$, so applying division by $s$ property gives $f(t) = -\\frac{2\\sinh t}{t}$. Hmm, but the answer choice is $\\frac{2\\sinh t}{t}$.\n\nLet me redo: $\\frac{1}{s+1} - \\frac{1}{s-1}$ inverts to $e^{-t} - e^t = -2\\sinh t$. The negative of this, $\\frac{2}{s^2-1}$, inverts to $2\\sinh t$.\n\nSo $f(t) = \\frac{2\\sinh t}{t}$.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
