    "prediction": "MiniMax-M3",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Looking at this FM receiver problem, I need to apply the output SNR formula for FM systems.\n\n**Setting up the calculation:**\n\nFor FM with sinusoidal modulation, the output SNR is:\n$$\\left(\\frac{S_o}{N_o}\\right)_{FM} = 3\\beta^2 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{S_i}{nf_m}\\right)$$\n\nConverting the input SNR from dB:\n$$\\frac{S_i}{nf_m} = 40 \\text{ dB} = 10^4$$\n\n**Computing each case:**\n\n- **β = 5:** SNR = 3(25)(10⁴) = 7.5 × 10⁵ → 10·log₁₀(7.5×10⁵) = **58.7 dB**\n\n- **β = 10:** SNR = 3(100)(10⁴) = 3 × 10⁶ → 10·log₁₀(3×10⁶) = **64.7 dB**\n\n- **β = 105:** SNR = 3(105²)(10⁴) = 3.3075 × 10⁸ → 10·log₁₀(3.3075×10⁸) = **85.185 dB**\n\nThese values match option A exactly.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
