    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to apply the Friis transmission equation for aligned half-wave dipoles at broadside (θ = 90°).\n\n**Step 1: Calculate wavelength**\nλ = c/f = (3×10⁸)/(200×10⁶) = 1.5 m\n\n**Step 2: Apply Friis transmission equation with gain for half-wave dipoles at θ = 90°**\n\nThe gain of a half-wave dipole is G_t = G_r = 1.64, and at θ = 90° (broadside), the full gain applies:\n\n$$P_r = P_t \\cdot G_t \\cdot G_r \\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\lambda}{4\\pi R}\\right)^2$$\n\n**Step 3: Plug in values**\n- P_t = 1000 W\n- G_t × G_r = (1.64)² = 2.6896\n- λ/(4πR) = 1.5/(4π × 500,000) = 1.5/(6.2832 × 10⁶) = 2.387 × 10⁻⁷\n- (λ/4πR)² = 5.697 × 10⁻¹⁴\n\n**Step 4: Calculate received power**\nP_r = 1000 × 2.6896 × 5.697 × 10⁻¹⁴ ≈ 1.53 × 10⁻¹⁰ W\n\n\\boxed{C}",
