    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Use Fouriertransformmethods to find the time-domain responseof a network having a system function [(j2\\omega) / (1 + 2j\\omega)], ifthe input is V(t) =cost (For asinusodialinputcost, the Fourier transform is \\pi[\\delta (\\omega + 1) + \\delta (\\omega - 1)] ).\n\nOptions: \nA. (4/5)cost - (2/5) sin t\nB. (3/4)cost - (1/4)sint\nC. (2/5)cost + (4/5) sin t\nD. cost + sint\nE. (3/5)cost + (1/5)sint\nF. (4/5)cost + (2/5) sin t\nG. (1/5)cost - (3/5)sint\nH. (1/2)cost + (1/2)sint\nI. (1/3)cost - (2/3)sint\nJ. (2/5)cost - (4/5) sin t\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "MiniMax-M3",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "# Solution\n\n**Setting up the problem:**\n\nThe system function is $H(j\\omega) = \\frac{j2\\omega}{1 + j2\\omega}$ and the input is $V(t) = \\cos t$.\n\n**Finding the output in frequency domain:**\n\n$$V_{out}(j\\omega) = H(j\\omega) \\cdot V(j\\omega) = \\frac{j2\\omega}{1 + j2\\omega} \\cdot \\pi[\\delta(\\omega+1) + \\delta(\\omega-1)]$$\n\n**Evaluating at ω = ±1:**\n\nAt $\\omega = 1$: $\\frac{j2}{1 + j2} = \\frac{j2(1-j2)}{(1+j2)(1-j2)} = \\frac{2+j2}{5} = \\frac{2}{5} + j\\frac{2}{5}$\n\nAt $\\omega = -1$: $\\frac{-j2}{1-j2} = \\frac{2}{5} - j\\frac{2}{5}$\n\n**Inverse Fourier Transform:**\n\n$$v_{out}(t) = \\pi \\cdot \\frac{2}{5}[\\delta(\\omega-1) + \\delta(\\omega+1)] + j\\pi \\cdot \\frac{2}{5}[\\delta(\\omega-1) - \\delta(\\omega+1)]$$\n\nUsing the inverse transforms:\n- $\\frac{1}{2\\pi}\\pi[\\delta(\\omega-1) + \\delta(\\omega+1)] = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos t$\n- $\\frac{1}{2\\pi}(j\\pi)[\\delta(\\omega-1) - \\delta(\\omega+1)] = \\frac{1}{2}\\sin t$\n\nTherefore: $v_{out}(t) = \\frac{4}{5}\\cos t + \\frac{2}{5}\\sin t$\n\n\\boxed{F}",
      "success": true,
