    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10298",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 6-pole 3-phase 60-cycle alternator has 12 slots per pole and four conductors per slot. The winding is five-sixths pitch. There are 2,500,000 maxwells (= 0.025 weber) entering the armature from each north pole, and this flux is sinusoidally distributed along the air gap. The armature coils are all connected in series. The winding is Y-connected. Determine the open-circuit emf of the alternator.\n\nOptions: \nA. 296 volts\nB. 480 volts\nC. 425 volts\nD. 350 volts\nE. 550 volts\nF. 600 volts\nG. 513 volts\nH. 250 volts\nI. 275 volts\nJ. 700 volts\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "MiniMax-M3",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to find the open-circuit EMF of the alternator.\n\n**Given information:**\n- 6 poles, 3-phase, 60 Hz\n- 12 slots per pole\n- 4 conductors per slot\n- Winding pitch = 5/6 (fractional pitch)\n- Total flux per pole = 2,500,000 maxwells = 0.025 Wb\n- Y-connected winding\n\n**Key parameters:**\n- Total conductors Z = 6 poles × 12 slots/pole × 4 conductors/slot = 288\n- Turns per phase T_ph = 288/(2×3) = 48\n- Frequency f = 60 Hz\n- Pitch factor K_p = sin(5/6 × 90°) = sin(75°) = 0.9659\n\n**Distribution factor calculation:**\n- Slots per pole per phase = 12/3 = 4\n- Slot angle β = 180°/12 = 15°\n- K_d = sin(qβ/2)/(q·sin(β/2)) = sin(30°)/(4·sin(7.5°)) = 0.5/0.5219 = 0.9577\n\n**Pitch factor:**\n- K_p = sin(5/6 × 90°) = sin(75°) = 0.9659\n\n**Winding factor:**\n- K_w = K_p × K_d = 0.9659 × 0.9577 = 0.9250\n\n**EMF calculation:**\n$$E_{ph} = 4.44 \\times f \\times \\Phi \\times T_{ph} \\times K_w$$\n$$E_{ph} = 4.44 \\times 60 \\times 0.025 \\times 48 \\times 0.9250 \\approx 295.7 \\text{ V}$$\n\nThis matches option A (296 volts).\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
