    "prediction": "MiniMax-M3",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The expression √(pq/n) is the formula for the standard error of a single proportion, where p and q are the population proportions (q = 1-p) and n is the sample size.\n\nThe standard error of the difference between two proportions would involve √(pq(1/n₁ + 1/n₂)), so this single-term expression with one n corresponds to one proportion.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is **C. Standard error of proportions**.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
