    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The text depicted in the right panel of the altarpiece in the Sint-Janshospitaal (St. John's Hospital) in Bruges is being written by its author, who is looking at an inset circle showing a red-cloaked man. This altarpiece is the work of Hans Memling, and the right panel shows Saint Luke writing the Gospel, with the red-cloaked figure traditionally identified as a portrait of either the patron or Memling himself.\n\n\\boxed{St. Luke}",
