      "generated_answer": "\n\\boxed{Democritus}  \nEpicurus calls upon Democritus' atomism to explain the material universe as formed by elemental particles rather than a divine being. This supports the idea that the universe operates according to natural laws without divine intervention. Lucretius later expands on these views to argue against fear of deities and death.",
