oanna manages to reach the shoreline, McLeach is swept over the waterfall to his death. Bernard dives into the water to save Cody, but every time he fails. His actions, however, buy Jake and Bianca enough time to free Marahute so they can save both Cody and Bernard.\nBernard, desperate to prevent any further incidents, proposes to Bianca, who eagerly and happily accepts while Jake salutes him with a newfound respect. All of them depart for Cody's home. Back at the nest, Marahute's eggs finally hatch, much to Wilbur's dismay.\n\nQuestion: What does McLeach think will happen to him if he finds an eagle like the one Cody did?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-R1-0528-Qwen3-8B",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\nMcLeach thinks capturing an eagle like the one Cody found will make him rich, as he previously profited from catching Marahute's mate. He is unaware of any negative consequences, focusing solely on the potential gain.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{He thinks he will become rich.}}",
