      "generated_answer": "\nThe economic shift from established wealth to industrial fortune causes the Amberson family's decline while the Morgan family prospers, impacting George's status and his relationship with Lucy. George's disapproval of his mother's affection for Lucy's father contrasts with the rising fortunes of the industrialists, further straining their connection. Ultimately, George's economic downfall diminishes his prospects for marrying Lucy, leading to the end of their relationship.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{The decline of the Amberson family's wealth due to industrialization contrasted with the prosperity of Lucy's family, and George's sabotage of his mother's relationship, causing his own fortunes to dwindle and making him less desirable to Lucy.}}",
