    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\nThe argument in the passage asserts that free African Americans are citizens with constitutional rights. The Supreme Court decision in *Dred Scott v. Sanford* (1857) directly contradicted this by ruling that African Americans were not citizens and had no rights as such, affirming the constitutionality of laws denying them citizenship. This decision stood in direct opposition to Garrison's position on constitutional guarantees.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
