      "generated_answer": "\nThe first passage undermines the assumption that European colonizers were uniformly eager to force their cultural norms on native populations, as Bentinck's conflicted decision to prohibit sati despite moral discomfort highlights a nuanced, less eager approach influenced by imperial concerns.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
